    <record id="skill_weather" model="ai.skill">
        <field name="name">Weather Forecast</field>
        <field
            name="description"
        >Get current weather and forecasts for any city using the web_fetch tool to query wttr.in (no API key required).</field>
        <field name="category_id" ref="category_weather" />
        <field name="priority">P1</field>
        <field name="source">custom</field>
        <field
            name="content"
        >You have access to the web_fetch tool which can fetch content from URLs.

Use it to get weather data from wttr.in (free, no API key needed).

How to get weather:

Current weather (compact):
  web_fetch(url="wttr.in/London?format=3")
  Response example: "London: Sunny 8C"

Full forecast:
  web_fetch(url="wttr.in/London?T")

Custom format:
  web_fetch(url="wttr.in/London?format=%l: %c %t %h %w")

Tips:
- URL-encode spaces: use wttr.in/New+York for "New York"
- Airport codes work: wttr.in/JFK
- Metric units: ?m (default)
- US units: ?u
- Today only: ?1

JSON format (for programmatic use) - Open-Meteo fallback:
  web_fetch(url="https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=51.5&amp;longitude=-0.12&amp;current_weather=true")

Coordinate lookup:
  web_fetch(url="https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search?name=London&amp;count=1")
  Returns latitude, longitude, country, etc.</field>
